From d4593a30136928882f57e343b8737f602a81888b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Rockefeller <alanrockefeller@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:01:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] CPU 4-state single precision: calls for different buffers
 may run concurrently

MrBayes (3.2.9-dikarya2) can compute the likelihoods of different MCMC chains
on different threads, one BEAGLE instance shared between them, each chain
using its own partials, matrices, scale buffers and eigen/weight/frequency
slots. Everything BEAGLE keeps per slot is then already private to a chain;
four things were not:

- the edge likelihood's per-pattern work arrays (integrationTmp,
  outLogLikelihoodsTmp), which getSiteLogLikelihoods then reads;
- the category rates, which beagleSetCategoryRates stores in one shared slot
  and updateTransitionMatrices reads;
- EigenDecompositionCube's matrixTmp.

These are now per thread (per instance): the edge likelihood writes into the
calling thread's arrays, getSiteLogLikelihoods returns the calling thread's
last result, and updateTransitionMatrices uses the rates the calling thread
last set (in a single-threaded caller, the same values as the shared slot,
which is still written, under a lock). The unthreaded 4-state edge likelihood now goes
through the same per-pattern job as the pattern-split one, with one chunk
covering every pattern; that is the code path already shown identical to the
original summation (exact threading, previous commit).

Nothing here changes a value: the same operations on the same operands in the
same order, only stored in a different place.
